.TH LLAMA\-STORY 1 "2026-11-17" "llama2c" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llama\-story \- a pocket story teller: a small language model continues the first words of a story
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llama\-story
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR steps ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR temperature ]
.RI [ "first words" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asks for the first words of a story (or takes them from the command line) and lets the model stories15M (15 million weights, trained on TinyStories) go on, about 3 tokens per second on the N900.
The model has 61 MB and is not in the package: the first time,
.B llama\-story
offers to download it from huggingface.co (with
.BR curl (1)) to
.IR ~/llama2c ,
checks its SHA\-256, and reuses it afterwards. When the download is refused or fails, or there is too little space, or with
.BR \-s ,
the tiny stories260K (1 MB) of the package tells the story.
.PP
The models only continue a text. They do not answer questions and do not hold a conversation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s
use the tiny model, without any download.
.TP
.BI \-n " steps"
the number of tokens (default 200).
.TP
.BI \-t " temperature"
the temperature (default 0.8; lower is more careful, higher more surprising).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLAMA2C_MODELS
where the downloaded model is kept (default
.IR ~/llama2c ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama2c (1)
.SH AUTHOR
elPytel; the engine and the models are by Andrej Karpathy (MIT licence).
